{"qid":"q127","family":"HB","refused":false,"reason_code":null,"answer":"The GSE/agency share was about 1.8 percentage points higher in 2026Q2 than at the start of the COVID-2020 window.\n\n- **2019Q4 (t0 of the COVID-19 recession window):** 45.2% of household mortgages plus consumer credit.\n- **2026Q2:** 47.0% of the same scope.\n\nThe gap is 47.01% minus 45.22%, or about 1.8 points. Both figures are shares of household 1–4 family mortgages plus consumer credit in the Fed's Z.1 data.","sources":[{"tool":"crisis_windows","args":{"metric":"share:gse_agency"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["FL154104015","FL313065105","FL403065105","FL413065105","FL213065103","FL763065105","FL753065103","FL743065103","FL473065100","FL673065105","FL643065173","FL153065103","FL103065105","FL113065103","FL543065105","FL573065103","FL223065143","FL613065105","FL313066220","FL403066005","FL763066005","FL473066000","FL673066000","FL613066005","FL103066003","FL113066003","FL163066223"],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"},{"tool":"holdings_by_bucket","args":{},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["FL154104015","FL153165105","FL153166000","FL313065105","FL403065105","FL413065105","FL213065103","FL763065105","FL753065103","FL743065103","FL473065100","FL673065105","FL643065173","FL153065103","FL103065105","FL113065103","FL543065105","FL573065103","FL223065143","FL613065105","FL313066220","FL403066005","FL763066005","FL473066000","FL673066000","FL613066005","FL103066003","FL113066003","FL163066223"],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"}],"usage":[{"turn":1,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":86,"cache_read_input_tokens":1456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":134,"cost_usd":0.0013486},{"turn":2,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":178,"cache_read_input_tokens":1590,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5043,"cost_usd":0.0145505}],"cost_usd":0.015899,"truncated":false,"rough_ok":true,"ts":"2026-11-06T05:30:26.174Z"}
{"qid":"q132","family":"CW","refused":false,"reason_code":null,"answer":"At the start of the Great Recession (GFC) window, 2007Q4, the home-backed collateral coverage ratio was about 2.20. This is collateral value divided by debt, so it is a ratio and not a share. Home collateral was worth roughly 2.2 times the home-backed debt.\n\nThe ratio then fell by about 0.21 after 4 quarters, 0.33 after 8 quarters and 0.34 after 16 quarters. These figures come from Z.1 data. The changes are descriptive and don't show that the crisis caused them.","sources":[{"tool":"crisis_windows","args":{"metric":"coverage:home_backed"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["FL154104015","FL313065105","FL403065105","FL413065105","FL213065103","FL763065105","FL753065103","FL743065103","FL473065100","FL673065105","FL643065173","FL153065103","FL103065105","FL113065103","FL543065105","FL573065103","FL223065143","FL613065105","FL313066220","FL403066005","FL763066005","FL473066000","FL673066000","FL613066005","FL103066003","FL113066003","FL163066223"],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"}],"usage":[{"turn":1,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":58,"cache_read_input_tokens":1456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":112,"cost_usd":0.0010136},{"turn":2,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":178,"cache_read_input_tokens":1568,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3217,"cost_usd":0.009983299999999999}],"cost_usd":0.010997,"truncated":false,"rough_ok":true,"ts":"2026-11-06T05:30:29.340Z"}
{"qid":"q136","family":"CW","refused":false,"reason_code":null,"answer":"The largest change in the public share 8 quarters after a window's start was **+8.44 percentage points**. It came in the Great Recession (GFC) window, which starts in 2007Q4. The public share was about 36.1% at the start of that window. This is Z.1 data on household 1–4 family mortgages plus consumer credit.\n\nThe next largest were the 1981–82 recession at +6.64 points and the 1990–91 recession at +5.41 points.\n\nThese are descriptive changes. The data doesn't show that the crisis caused them.","sources":[{"tool":"crisis_windows","args":{"metric":"public_share"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["FL154104015","FL313065105","FL403065105","FL413065105","FL213065103","FL763065105","FL753065103","FL743065103","FL473065100","FL673065105","FL643065173","FL153065103","FL103065105","FL113065103","FL543065105","FL573065103","FL223065143","FL613065105","FL313066220","FL403066005","FL763066005","FL473066000","FL673066000","FL613066005","FL103066003","FL113066003","FL163066223"],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"}],"usage":[{"turn":1,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":53,"cache_read_input_tokens":1456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":112,"cost_usd":0.0009636},{"turn":2,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":172,"cache_read_input_tokens":1568,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3187,"cost_usd":0.009848299999999999}],"cost_usd":0.010812,"truncated":false,"rough_ok":true,"ts":"2026-11-06T05:30:32.371Z"}
{"qid":"q142","family":"CW","refused":false,"reason_code":null,"answer":"The home-backed collateral coverage ratio was about **1.36 higher** in 2026Q2 than at the start of the GFC window.\n\n- 2026Q2: 3.562, a ratio of aggregate collateral value to aggregate debt.\n- 2007Q4 (t0): 2.200.\n- Difference: 3.5624 − 2.2001 = **+1.3623**.\n\nThis is a Z.1 sector-level aggregate. It isn't a per-loan loan-to-value measure.","sources":[{"tool":"crisis_windows","args":{"metric":"coverage:home_backed"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["FL154104015","FL313065105","FL403065105","FL413065105","FL213065103","FL763065105","FL753065103","FL743065103","FL473065100","FL673065105","FL643065173","FL153065103","FL103065105","FL113065103","FL543065105","FL573065103","FL223065143","FL613065105","FL313066220","FL403066005","FL763066005","FL473066000","FL673066000","FL613066005","FL103066003","FL113066003","FL163066223"],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"},{"tool":"collateral_coverage","args":{"end":"2026Q2"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["FL153165105","FL153166100","FL153166220","FL153166400","FL153166205","FL155035015","FL155111005"],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"}],"usage":[{"turn":1,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":110,"cache_read_input_tokens":1456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":138,"cost_usd":0.0015986},{"turn":2,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":162,"cache_read_input_tokens":1594,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4469,"cost_usd":0.0129559}],"cost_usd":0.014554,"truncated":false,"rough_ok":true,"ts":"2026-11-06T05:30:35.995Z"}
{"qid":"q145","family":"CW","refused":false,"reason_code":null,"answer":"The GFC 2007 crisis window starts in 2007Q4. In that quarter, the New York Fed Consumer Credit Panel shows a household mortgage balance of **$9,101 billion**, or about $9.1 trillion.\n\nThis figure is from the NY Fed's credit-bureau data. It uses a different definition from the Federal Reserve's Z.1 accounts, so don't compare it with Z.1 totals. The NY Fed reports HELOCs separately, at $647 billion in the same quarter.","sources":[{"tool":"crisis_windows","args":{},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["FL154104015","FL313065105","FL403065105","FL413065105","FL213065103","FL763065105","FL753065103","FL743065103","FL473065100","FL673065105","FL643065173","FL153065103","FL103065105","FL113065103","FL543065105","FL573065103","FL223065143","FL613065105","FL313066220","FL403066005","FL763066005","FL473066000","FL673066000","FL613066005","FL103066003","FL113066003","FL163066223"],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"},{"tool":"nyfed_by_type","args":{"start":"2007Q4","end":"2007Q4"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["NYFED_HHDC"],"vintage":"2026-10-27","source":"nyfed"}],"usage":[{"turn":1,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":101,"cache_read_input_tokens":1456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":117,"cost_usd":0.0014560999999999999},{"turn":2,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":81,"cache_read_input_tokens":1573,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3235,"cost_usd":0.009058799999999999},{"turn":3,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":169,"cache_read_input_tokens":4808,"cache_creation_input_tokens":889,"cost_usd":0.0043973}],"cost_usd":0.014912,"truncated":false,"rough_ok":true,"ts":"2026-11-06T05:30:40.618Z"}
{"qid":"q150","family":"CC","refused":false,"reason_code":null,"answer":"In 2026Q2, the home-backed collateral value was about **$49.8 trillion**. That is $49,791,678 million in the Z.1 data, at end of quarter and not seasonally adjusted.\n\nThis is the value of household real estate in the Z.1 data, matched against $14.0 trillion of home-backed debt. That gives an aggregate coverage ratio of about 3.56. It is a sector-wide figure, not a loan-by-loan loan-to-value measure.\n\nThe data doesn't say that this entire $49.8 trillion value \"backs\" mortgages. It is the total collateral value for the home-backed class, which includes all owner-occupied real estate.","sources":[{"tool":"data_coverage","args":{},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":[],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"},{"tool":"collateral_coverage","args":{"end":"2026Q2","start":"2026Q2"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["FL153165105","FL153166100","FL153166220","FL153166400","FL153166205","FL155035015","FL155111005"],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"}],"usage":[{"turn":1,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":105,"cache_read_input_tokens":1456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":111,"cost_usd":0.0014811},{"turn":2,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":216,"cache_read_input_tokens":1567,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2146,"cost_usd":0.0076857}],"cost_usd":0.009167,"truncated":false,"rough_ok":true,"ts":"2026-11-06T05:30:44.556Z"}
{"qid":"q154","family":"CC","refused":false,"reason_code":null,"answer":"Owner-occupied real estate value grew about 174.5% from 2011Q4 to 2026Q2. The data uses the Z.1 home-collateral value, which I'm treating as the owner-occupied real estate series.\n\n- **2011Q4:** $18,135,722 million, about $18.1 trillion.\n- **2026Q2:** $49,791,678 million, about $49.8 trillion.\n\nThat is roughly 2.75 times the 2011Q4 level. These are nominal dollars, with no adjustment for inflation. They are end-of-quarter levels, not seasonally adjusted.","sources":[{"tool":"data_coverage","args":{},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":[],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"},{"tool":"collateral_coverage","args":{"start":"2011Q4","end":"2026Q2"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["FL153165105","FL153166100","FL153166220","FL153166400","FL153166205","FL155035015","FL155111005"],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"}],"usage":[{"turn":1,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":28,"cache_read_input_tokens":1456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":109,"cost_usd":0.0007061},{"turn":2,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":99,"cache_read_input_tokens":1565,"cache_creation_input_tokens":870,"cost_usd":0.0033255},{"turn":3,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":372,"cache_read_input_tokens":2435,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27472,"cost_usd":0.0726475}],"cost_usd":0.076679,"truncated":false,"rough_ok":true,"ts":"2026-11-06T05:30:49.286Z"}
{"qid":"q157","family":"CC","refused":false,"reason_code":null,"answer":"In 2026Q2, Z.1 vehicle-backed household debt was about $1,574.75 billion. That is $1,574,750 million. The NY Fed's auto loan balance was $1,713 billion.\n\nZ.1 minus NY Fed is about **–$138.25 billion**. Z.1 is lower.\n\nThe two sources define and measure debt differently, so they don't reconcile. Part of this gap is probably definitional. The Z.1 vehicle-backed figure is a collateral class, not a published auto-loan line.","sources":[{"tool":"collateral_coverage","args":{"start":"2026Q2","end":"2026Q2"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["FL153165105","FL153166100","FL153166220","FL153166400","FL153166205","FL155035015","FL155111005"],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"},{"tool":"nyfed_by_type","args":{"start":"2026Q2","end":"2026Q2"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["NYFED_HHDC"],"vintage":"2026-10-27","source":"nyfed"},{"tool":"data_coverage","args":{},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":[],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"}],"usage":[{"turn":1,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":183,"cache_read_input_tokens":1456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":142,"cost_usd":0.0023385999999999997},{"turn":2,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":173,"cache_read_input_tokens":1598,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3038,"cost_usd":0.009488799999999999}],"cost_usd":0.011827,"truncated":false,"rough_ok":false,"ts":"2026-11-06T05:30:53.110Z"}
{"qid":"q161","family":"NY","refused":false,"reason_code":null,"answer":"The New York Fed's Consumer Credit Panel shows a credit card balance of **$1,263 billion** in 2026Q2. That is about $1.26 trillion.\n\nThis is credit bureau data. It uses a different definition from the Federal Reserve's Z.1 accounts, so don't compare it with Z.1 totals. The data isn't seasonally adjusted.","sources":[{"tool":"nyfed_by_type","args":{"start":"2026Q2","end":"2026Q2"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["NYFED_HHDC"],"vintage":"2026-10-27","source":"nyfed"}],"usage":[{"turn":1,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":81,"cache_read_input_tokens":1456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":102,"cost_usd":0.0012185999999999998},{"turn":2,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":122,"cache_read_input_tokens":1558,"cache_creation_input_tokens":872,"cost_usd":0.0035598}],"cost_usd":0.004778,"truncated":false,"rough_ok":true,"ts":"2026-11-06T05:30:56.443Z"}
{"qid":"q166","family":"NY","refused":false,"reason_code":null,"answer":"In the NY Fed Consumer Credit Panel, the student loan serious-delinquency transition rate peaked in **2025Q4** at about **16.19%**. This is the share of student loan balances that newly became 90+ days delinquent, annualized and not seasonally adjusted. The series covers 2004Q1 to 2026Q2.\n\nThe rate was 14.26% in 2025Q3 and 10.86% in 2026Q1. It was 7.83% in the latest quarter, 2026Q2.\n\nThis is NY Fed credit-bureau data. It is not comparable with the Federal Reserve's Z.1 figures.","sources":[{"tool":"nyfed_by_type","args":{},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["NYFED_HHDC"],"vintage":"2026-10-27","source":"nyfed"},{"tool":"data_coverage","args":{},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":[],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"},{"tool":"nyfed_by_type","args":{"start":"2003Q1","end":"2026Q2"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["NYFED_HHDC"],"vintage":"2026-10-27","source":"nyfed"}],"usage":[{"turn":1,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":56,"cache_read_input_tokens":1456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":107,"cost_usd":0.0009811},{"turn":2,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":101,"cache_read_input_tokens":1563,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1740,"cost_usd":0.0055203000000000006},{"turn":3,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":206,"cache_read_input_tokens":3303,"cache_creation_input_tokens":36606,"cost_usd":0.0939093}],"cost_usd":0.100411,"truncated":false,"rough_ok":true,"ts":"2026-11-06T05:31:01.335Z"}
{"qid":"q172","family":"NY","refused":false,"reason_code":null,"answer":"The GFC 2007 window starts in 2007Q4. Eight quarters later is 2009Q4.\n\nIn 2009Q4, the NY Fed Consumer Credit Panel shows **10.96%** of credit card balances newly moving into serious delinquency (90+ days). This is an annualized rate, as the NY Fed publishes it.\n\nIn 2007Q4 the rate was 6.75%.\n\nThe built-in crisis-window tool only covers the Z.1 public share, not NY Fed data. I looked up the quarters directly instead. NY Fed figures use different definitions from Z.1, so don't compare the two.","sources":[{"tool":"crisis_windows","args":{},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["FL154104015","FL313065105","FL403065105","FL413065105","FL213065103","FL763065105","FL753065103","FL743065103","FL473065100","FL673065105","FL643065173","FL153065103","FL103065105","FL113065103","FL543065105","FL573065103","FL223065143","FL613065105","FL313066220","FL403066005","FL763066005","FL473066000","FL673066000","FL613066005","FL103066003","FL113066003","FL163066223"],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"},{"tool":"nyfed_by_type","args":{"start":"2007Q1","end":"2010Q1"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["NYFED_HHDC"],"vintage":"2026-10-27","source":"nyfed"}],"usage":[{"turn":1,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":227,"cache_read_input_tokens":1456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":118,"cost_usd":0.0027186},{"turn":2,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":203,"cache_read_input_tokens":1574,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8926,"cost_usd":0.0245064}],"cost_usd":0.027225,"truncated":false,"rough_ok":true,"ts":"2026-11-06T05:31:05.851Z"}
{"qid":"q175","family":"NY","refused":false,"reason_code":null,"answer":"I can't give you a valid ratio. The two sources define debt differently and don't reconcile, so dividing one by the other would be misleading.\n\nFor 2007Q4, the two figures are:\n- **NY Fed Consumer Credit Panel:** HELOC balances were $647 billion.\n- **Z.1 Financial Accounts:** home-backed household debt was $10,577,134 million, or about $10.58 trillion. That was 80.2% of the Z.1 scope, which is a share.\n\nThe Z.1 scope also excludes HELOCs as a separate line.\n\nInstead, I can compare within one source. For example, I can compare the NY Fed's HELOC balance to its own mortgage balance, which was $9,101 billion in 2007Q4.","sources":[{"tool":"nyfed_by_type","args":{"start":"2007Q4","end":"2007Q4"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["NYFED_HHDC"],"vintage":"2026-10-27","source":"nyfed"},{"tool":"collateral_coverage","args":{"start":"2007Q4","end":"2007Q4"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["FL153165105","FL153166100","FL153166220","FL153166400","FL153166205","FL155035015","FL155111005"],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"}],"usage":[{"turn":1,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":254,"cache_read_input_tokens":1456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":114,"cost_usd":0.0029786},{"turn":2,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":244,"cache_read_input_tokens":1570,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2264,"cost_usd":0.008261}],"cost_usd":0.01124,"truncated":false,"rough_ok":false,"ts":"2026-11-06T05:31:10.703Z"}
{"qid":"q179","family":"RG","refused":false,"reason_code":null,"answer":"The public-share series runs from 1951Q4 to 2026Q2 (Z.1, quarterly). Counting both end quarters, that is 299 quarters, or about 74 and a half years. The coverage tool gives only the start and end dates, so the count assumes there are no gaps in between.","sources":[{"tool":"data_coverage","args":{},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":[],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"}],"usage":[{"turn":1,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":28,"cache_read_input_tokens":1456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":89,"cost_usd":0.0006561000000000001},{"turn":2,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":217,"cache_read_input_tokens":1545,"cache_creation_input_tokens":870,"cost_usd":0.0045035}],"cost_usd":0.00516,"truncated":false,"rough_ok":true,"ts":"2026-11-06T05:31:14.157Z"}
{"qid":"q183","family":"RG","refused":false,"reason_code":null,"answer":"In 2011Q4, about **5.02 percentage points** of household mortgage and consumer credit were held by public holders other than the GSE/agency bucket. This is the project's validated claim (E1-q183, status PASS).\n\nThe two shares are in the same Z.1 scope:\n- The public share was 49.2% of that scope.\n- GSEs and agency pools held 44.2%.\n- The rest of the public share is the federal government (direct) at 4.1% and state and local governments at 0.9%.\n\nThese are shares of the total, shown as percentages.","sources":[{"tool":"lookup_claim","args":{"text_or_id":"public share 2011Q4 GSE agency"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["(+","FL153165105","FL153166000","FL154104015","FL213065103","FL313065105","FL313066220","FL403065105","FL403066005","FL413065105","FL893065105","bucket","holder","public","series)"],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"},{"tool":"holdings_by_bucket","args":{"quarter":"2011Q4"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["FL154104015","FL153165105","FL153166000","FL313065105","FL403065105","FL413065105","FL213065103","FL763065105","FL753065103","FL743065103","FL473065100","FL673065105","FL643065173","FL153065103","FL103065105","FL113065103","FL543065105","FL573065103","FL223065143","FL613065105","FL313066220","FL403066005","FL763066005","FL473066000","FL673066000","FL613066005","FL103066003","FL113066003","FL163066223"],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"},{"tool":"public_share","args":{"start":"2011Q4","end":"2011Q4"},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":["FL154104015","FL153165105","FL153166000","FL313065105","FL403065105","FL413065105","FL213065103","FL313066220","FL403066005"],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"}],"usage":[{"turn":1,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":196,"cache_read_input_tokens":1456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":115,"cost_usd":0.0024010999999999998},{"turn":2,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":177,"cache_read_input_tokens":1571,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4640,"cost_usd":0.0135311}],"cost_usd":0.015932,"truncated":false,"rough_ok":true,"ts":"2026-11-06T05:31:18.043Z"}
