{"qid":"q190","family":"UN","refused":false,"reason_code":null,"answer":"I can't tell you the credit card serious-delinquency transition rate for 2026Q4. That would be a forecast. The NY Fed data I have ends at 2026Q2, so 2026Q4 isn't in it.\n\nI can give you the most recent actual figure, for 2026Q2. I can also show how the rate has moved over earlier quarters. Would you like either of those? Keep in mind that this is New York Fed Consumer Credit Panel data, not Z.1 data. The two sources define things differently.","sources":[{"tool":"data_coverage","args":{},"ok":true,"refused":false,"series_ids":[],"vintage":"2026-09-11","source":"z1"}],"usage":[{"turn":1,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":84,"cache_read_input_tokens":1456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":104,"cost_usd":0.0012536},{"turn":2,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":164,"cache_read_input_tokens":1560,"cache_creation_input_tokens":926,"cost_usd":0.004115}],"cost_usd":0.005369,"truncated":false,"rough_ok":false,"ts":"2026-11-06T05:31:22.292Z"}
